    "congress": 118,
    "constitutionalAuthorityStatementText": "<pre>\n[Congressional Record Volume 170, Number 54 (Friday, March 29, 2024)]\n[House]\nFrom the Congressional Record Online through the Government Publishing Office [<a href=\"https://www.gpo.gov\">www.gpo.gov</a>]\nBy Mr. CORREA:\nH.R. 7832.\nCongress has the power to enact this legislation pursuant\nto the following:\nArticle I, Section 8, Clause 18\nThe single subject of this legislation is:\nAddress capability gaps in border security operations by\nrequiring the Secretary of Homeland Security to submit a plan\nto Congress to identify, integrate and deploy innovative\ntechnologies like artificial intelligence (AI), machine\nlearning, and nanotechnology.\n[Page H2129]\n</pre>",
